alwaysApply: true
---

Entities

Base currencies: INR, USDT

Symbols: e.g., BTC/INR, BTC/USDT, and USDT/INR

Legs:

Straight: INR→USDT (buy USDT/INR ask) → COIN (buy COIN/USDT ask) → INR (sell COIN/INR bid)

Reverse: INR→COIN (buy COIN/INR ask) → USDT (sell COIN/USDT bid) → INR (sell USDT/INR bid)

Triangle enumeration

For each coin X that has both X/INR and X/USDT, triangles are:

TriangleStraight(X) = [USDT/INR (buy), X/USDT (buy), X/INR (sell)]

TriangleReverse(X) = [X/INR (buy), X/USDT (sell), USDT/INR (sell)]

Fees, precision, constraints

Per-market:

pricePrecision, quantityPrecision, minQty, minNotional, maxQty (from markets metadata).

Fee model:

Start with taker fee on all three legs (conservative).

Parametrize maker/taker per leg (future).

Edge calculation (per 03-market-model formulas)
Straight
usdt = inr0 / usdtinr.ask * (1 - fee_taker)
coin = usdt / xusdt.ask * (1 - fee_taker)
inr_final = coin * xinr.bid * (1 - fee_taker)
edge = inr_final / inr0 - 1

Reverse
coin = inr0 / xinr.ask * (1 - fee_taker)
usdt = coin * xusdt.bid * (1 - fee_taker)
inr_final = usdt * usdtinr.bid * (1 - fee_taker)
edge = inr_final / inr0 - 1


Apply rounding/precision at each leg’s quantity BEFORE computing the next leg. Enforce minQty and minNotional for each trade.

Liquidity & slippage guard

Require cumulative depth at least qty_needed * (1 + slip_buffer) within top K levels.

Maintain depth snapshot up to K=5; if insufficient, skip signal.